   "text": {
    "L1": "When numbers are close to tens, change them into friendly numbers.",
    "L2": "For 68 plus 29, use 30: 68 plus 30 is 98, then take away 1 to get 97.",
    "L3": "To add 9, add 10 and take away 1, because 10 is one too many.",
    "L4": "So 57 plus 9 is 57 plus 10 minus 1, which is 66.",
    "L5": "For subtraction, add the same number to both numbers. The gap stays the same.",
    "L6": "That is why 63 minus 28 equals 65 minus 30, and both differences are 35.",
    "L7": "The equals sign means both sides have the same value, not just that an answer comes next.",
    "L8": "Now use the same-difference trick for 82 minus 39."
   },
